  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Resonance Room",
    "overview": "One acoustic guitar is the spatial centre of a saturated cobalt room. A black-finish instrument, chrome details and porcelain typography make the object tangible; close views connect strings, fretting and anchors to physical actions. The current original procedural model represents the user's Yamaha FS80C Black with an illustrative concert-cutaway silhouette. It is a teaching representation, not a manufacturer CAD asset.\n\nThe learning workspace carries the same cobalt into quieter porcelain surfaces, graphite text and compact controls. Bricolage Grotesque gives large teaching statements presence; Rethink Sans keeps instructions and repeated practice easy to scan. The contrast between the spatial entrance and the task desk is deliberate. Clear actions, restrained boundaries and useful diagrams carry the experience.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A persistent instrument world controlled by native scroll.",
      "Cobalt navigation and action states across pale task surfaces.",
      "Compact expressive headings with calm, readable instruction text.",
      "Motion tied to navigation, explicit sound actions and state changes.",
      "Direct access to practice, with still and poster alternatives to the world."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Action Continuity Rule",
        "body": "Cobalt connects the immersive world to practice actions and selected states; the black instrument finish remains an object treatment.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Rhythm Rule",
